<title>USA: USDA to hold briefing on EU/U.S. meat trade row.</title>
<headline>USDA to hold briefing on EU/U.S. meat trade row.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said it will hold a briefing on the meat trade row with the European Union at 3 p.m. EST (2000 GMT) on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Earlier this week, Washington and Brussels took separate actions that would halt hundreds of millions of dollars worth of transatlantic meat and poultry trade after meat inspection talks between the two sides failed to reach an agreement.</p>
<p>USDA said senior trade advisor Paul Drazek will be at the briefing, among other department officials.</p>
<p>((-- Leila Corcoran, Washington Commodities 202-898-8394))</p>
</text>
